# The release archive is what the DOI points at. It should contain what an
# Excel user actually needs -- the add-in, the module source, the licence, the
# changelog and the rendered manual, all at the top level -- and nothing that
# only matters to someone working inside the repository.
#
# Two generated files are deliberately NOT export-ignored. EGAMMA.xlam is the
# add-in the README tells people to install. EGAMMA-VBA-manual.pdf is the
# documentation in the only form this audience can use; both are committed at
# the repository root so that they appear at the root of the archive, and so of
# the archival deposit made from it.
#
# Everything under docs/ is the Sphinx machinery that produces the manual.
# It stays in the repository and out of the archive.

docs   export-ignore
.git*  export-ignore

# Zenodo deposition metadata, read by Zenodo from the repository rather than
# from the archive.
.zenodo.json export-ignore
